From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:44:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: put the SD reader's root port back when
 the reader powers up

With the slot empty the J604's SD card reader is powered down, its port
reset with it, and that reset takes the root port's configuration too.
When the reader is powered up again (a card, or every system sleep,
which powers it up first), the root port reads its reset values: bus
numbers 0, no memory window, memory decoding off. The rescan renumbers
the bus but sets up no window behind a bridge that is already enabled,
so every read of the reader's BAR came back all ones and sdhci logged
"Reset 0x1 never completed" with an all-ones register dump, before and
after each sleep (1.922, first full deep wake).

Save the root port's state at the power-down, while it still answers,
and restore it after the link is back and before the rescan, as the
radio's Neo path does before its own link. On by default;
pcie_apple.t8132_sd_restore_root=0 turns it off.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index 63f3de3eb8..366d422688 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -88,6 +88,10 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops apple_pcie_sd_param_ops = {
 	.get = param_get_bool,
 };
 module_param_cb(t8132_sd_port_off, &apple_pcie_sd_param_ops, &t8132_sd_port_off, 0644);
+static bool t8132_sd_restore_root = true;
+module_param(t8132_sd_restore_root, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_sd_restore_root,
+		 "J604: put the SD reader's root port config back after powering the reader up (default on)");
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132_sd_port_off,
 		 "J604: power the SD card reader's port down while the slot is empty and up again when a card is inserted, as macOS does (default on)");
 
@@ -2995,6 +2999,9 @@ static void apple_pcie_sd_power_down(struct apple_pcie *pcie, struct apple_pcie_
 	 */
 	if (rp && !port->sd_rp_held && pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&rp->dev) >= 0)
 		port->sd_rp_held = pci_dev_get(rp);
+	/* The port's reset takes the root port's config too: kept for the power-up. */
+	if (port->sd_rp_held)
+		pci_save_state(port->sd_rp_held);
 	if (rp && rp->subordinate)
 		list_for_each_entry_safe_reverse(dev, tmp, &rp->subordinate->devices, bus_list)
 			pci_stop_and_remove_bus_device(dev);
@@ -3071,6 +3078,14 @@ static int apple_pcie_sd_power_up(struct apple_pcie *pcie, struct apple_pcie_por
 	}
 
 	pci_lock_rescan_remove();
+	/*
+	 * The root port comes back at its reset values: bus numbers 0, no window, memory
+	 * decoding off. The PCI core renumbers the bus but sets no window up for a bridge it
+	 * has enabled, so every read of the reader's BAR came back all ones. As the radio's
+	 * Neo path does before its link, the state saved at the power-down goes back first.
+	 */
+	if (port->sd_rp_held && READ_ONCE(t8132_sd_restore_root))
+		pci_restore_state(port->sd_rp_held);
 	if (bridge->bus)
 		pci_rescan_bus(bridge->bus);
 	pci_unlock_rescan_remove();
-- 
2.43.0

